4. Make addons: mods, datapacks, resource packs and Builder theme packs that
   work with, depend on or change the Mod. You may read and compile against
   our source code to do this. Resource packs may include edited versions of
   our textures, models and sounds. Your addon is your own work under your
   own license, but it may not copy our code beyond what is needed to hook
   into it (names, IDs, method signatures).
5. Help out: report bugs and share ideas or translations by opening an issue
   on GitHub. Pull requests with code or assets are welcome too; you may fork
   this repository on GitHub to make one. We decide what gets merged.
6. Change it for yourself: private changes for your own use, as long as you
   do not share the changed Mod.

YOU MAY NOT, WITHOUT OUR WRITTEN PERMISSION:
a. Re-upload the Mod, changed or unchanged, as its own download anywhere
